    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0608" n="528" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.35E1/144</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1236</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-05-11">May 11, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Embassy’s despatch
                    No. 1897 of January 3, 1936,<anchor n="15" xml:id="d437-f1"/> enclosing an
                    informal note from Mr. Ashton-Gwatkin<anchor n="16" xml:id="d437-f2"/> regarding
                    the possible International Sugar Conference, there is enclosed herewith a
                    memorandum approved by the President, a copy of which it is desired be left with
                    the Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs or the Permanent Under Secretary of
                    the Foreign Office. You will please state that this memorandum is for the
                    confidential information of the Foreign Office and is not to be made public
                    without the consent of this Government, which cannot be given at this time.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d437-a1.xml" xpointer="d437-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d437-f1" n="15" xml:id="d437-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see telegram No. 4, January 3, 4 p.m., <ref target="#pg521">p.
                        521</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d437-f2" n="16" xml:id="d437-f2-content">
                <p>Frank T. A. Ashton-Gwatkin, Counselor for Economic Relations in the British
                    Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
